{
  "title": "Rig kit: TPU phone cases with swappable mounts, shoe foot and GoPro heads",
  "summary": "TPU cases for a Xiaomi 12 Pro and an iPhone 13 mini with a swappable plate (cold-shoe receiver or GoPro prongs), a cold-shoe foot with lock wheel, GoPro 3- and 2-prong heads and an accessory shoe. Everything uses GoPro and cold-shoe standards.",
  "status": "preview",
  "date": "2026-11-27",
  "material": "TPU 95A cases (Gås); PETG plates, feet, heads and wheel for use, PLA fit test (TNT). Hardware from the kit: M5 x 20 and M3 x 16 countersunk screws with nuts, M4 x 16 countersunk as a steel core in the stud.",
  "notes": "Round 3, after three review rounds by four independent reviewers (functionality, durability, ergonomics, aesthetics): all PASS; 107 self-checks, 101 pass, 6 near-misses that physical tests settle (stud bending at 10 g, knob glue, weight, plate coverage on the Xiaomi, a mated GoPro part pointing straight back). How it works: the PLA/PETG plate sits in a pocket inside the 3.0 mm case back, held by the phone, and fills a rounded window flush with the case. The shoe plate is a cold-shoe receiver: drop the foot into the channel, slide it toward the phone top, lock the wheel. The foot's key takes head3 (3-prong) or head2 (2-prong, for standard GoPro mounts), locked with an M3 pin; head3 can't point its knob toward the phone top, so nothing of the mount shows in the ultra-wide camera. The prong plates give a low GoPro mount (landscape or portrait). Cases have raised button covers, corner bumpers with air channels and lens rings 0.5 mm inside the back. iPhone data is Apple's drawing; the Xiaomi comes from a photo (+-1.5 mm), so the TPU bands (button stretch + camera edge, 1.5 h) print first as a fit test. Infill: functional parts 6 walls, 40 % gyroid. Plates: Gås TPU bands 1 h 26 min / 19 g; Gås TPU cases 4 h 34 min / 59 g; TNT PLA fit set 2 h 51 min / 47 g; TNT PETG grey 1 h 19 min / 19 g; TNT PETG orange 2 h 51 min / 63 g. No supports anywhere.",
